Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Everything downstream already existed: SvgGraphicsTeaVM takes a background
color and paints a style plus a full viewBox rectangle, mirroring the skip
rules of SvgGraphics.paintBackcolor. It just never received the color, because
buildSvg only asked the TextBlock, and the document background set by
skinparam backgroundColor or by a theme never surfaces there.

Read it from the merged root.document style via calculateBackColor(), exactly
where ImageBuilder.styled() gets it for the Java build.

The diversion only happens for a background that should actually be painted,
judged on the plain (light mapped) color so the decision is mode independent:
transparent and the skin default of white keep painting nothing, in dark mode
too, where the skin pairs white with a dark value but the page has always
supplied its own backdrop. Falling through also keeps the historic WHITE and
BLACK fallback as the contrast reference for automatic colors. Two earlier
shapes of this change were caught by the RED checks: diverting
unconditionally, and judging the mode mapped color, both of which made the
dark mode control start painting a background it never painted before.

check-background.js is now fully green, check-themes.js stays green, and the
22 corpus diagrams (which use the default background) are byte-identical to
the previous build.
